  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was a study in contrasts across your footprint, and it surfaces a real operational concern you need to address.\n\nPort Washington is underperforming. Revenue dropped 9% yesterday against a DOW-adjusted expectation miss of 9.2%\u2014this is real, not calendar. Core grooming revenue fell 12% week-over-week while add-on attach actually improved to 59%, so the problem isn't upsell discipline; it's raw grooming volume. You ran 4 groomers at $514/groomer (above your 30-day baseline of $466), which is encouraging productivity, but bather hours came in at 4.5 against a 5.7-day average\u2014that's a 21% shortfall that's constraining throughput. MTD you're down 7% in revenue and 3% in appointments, but critically, you're down 1 groomer-day per day versus September and your per-groomer productivity is down $48/day. This is a capacity ramp problem, not a demand problem.\n\nHicksville is the bright spot. Yesterday's 134% revenue jump was real\u2014DOW-adjusted you're +3% MTD, and more importantly, you're running 5 groomers at $489/groomer (up $73 from your 30-day baseline of $416). You've added meaningful grooming capacity and it's converting. MTD appointments are up 24% and revenue is up 25%. This is what happens when you staff for demand. The risk: tomorrow you have zero groomers scheduled and zero bathers for the next 7 days. That's a planning gap that will crater next week's numbers.\n\nGlen Cove is too early to read, but the signal is concerning: you have zero groomer-days scheduled for the next 7 days. Yesterday's 71% jump was against a low comp and only 2 groomers. This location needs a staffing strategy or it will remain a low-productivity satellite.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port Washington runs 4 groomers/8.0h bathers today and 1 groomer/15.0h bathers tomorrow; Hicksville runs 4 groomers/0.0h bathers today and 0 tomorrow; across both stores next 7 days you have 58 groomer-days scheduled and 83 bather hours\u2014you need to front-load Port Washington groomer coverage and clarify Hicksville's week-ahead staffing immediately.**"
